WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.272
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC) ♪

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.510
- (HORSE NICKERING)
- My beloved wife!

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.048
I've missed you terribly.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.454
Thank you for returning
Lady Bolton safely.

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:24.457
Now, dismount and
kneel before me.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.726
Surrender your army,
and proclaim me

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.128
the true Lord of Winterfell
and Warden of the North.

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:31.764
I will pardon you for deserting
the Night's Watch.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.368
I will pardon these treasonous
Lords for betraying my house.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.740
Come, bastard.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:43.142
You don't have the men,

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:46.279
you don't have the horses,
and you don't have Winterfell.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.249
Why lead those poor souls
into slaughter?

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.285
There's no need for a battle.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.156
Get off your horse. Kneel.

00:00:58.223 --> 00:00:59.526
I am a man of mercy.

00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:06.399
You're right.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.868
There's no need for a battle.

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:12.739
Thousands of men
don't need to die.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.509
Only one of us.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.083
Let's end this the old way.
You against me.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.692
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:38.865
I keep hearing stories
about you, bastard.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.899
The way people in the North
talk about you.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.802
You're the greatest swordsman
who ever walked.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.872
Maybe you are that good.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.541
Maybe not.

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:51.444
I don't know if I'd beat you,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.347
but I know that my army
would beat yours.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.318
I have 6000 men. You have what?

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.753
Half that?

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.656
- Not even?
- Aye. You have the numbers.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.660
Will your men want to fight
for you, when they hear

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.062
you wouldn't fight for them?

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:20.807
(CHUCKLES)
He's good. Very good.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.710
Tell me. Will you let
your little brother die

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.046
because you're
too proud to surrender?

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:28.982
How do we know you have him?

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:43.395
(THUD)

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:44.497
(HORSE NEIGHING)

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.442
RAMSAY:
Now, if you want to say--

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.478
You're going to die tomorrow,
Lord Bolton.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.117
Sleep well!

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.989
(HORSE GALLOPING)

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.527
She's a fine woman, your sister.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.097
I look forward to having her
back in my bed.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.100
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC) ♪

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.069
And, you're all
fine-looking men.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.772
My dogs are desperate
to meet you.

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:29.542
I haven't fed them for
seven days. They're ravenous.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.812
I wonder which parts
they'll try first.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.614
Your eyes...

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.716
Your balls!

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.353
We'll find out soon enough.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:45.892
In the morning then, bastard.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.966
- (CLIP CLOP OF HOOVES)
- (HORSES NICKERING)

